# Git Workflow Rules - Gitflow Process

## Branch Structure

### Main Branches (Permanent)
- **`main`** (or `master`): Production-ready code only. Never commit directly to main.
- **`develop`**: Integration branch for features. Latest development changes.

### Supporting Branches (Temporary)

#### Feature Branches
- **Naming**: `feature/<ticket-number>-<short-description>` or `feature/<short-description>`
- **Examples**: 
  - `feature/RAG-123-add-document-upload`
  - `feature/fastapi-backend-setup`
- **Branch from**: `develop`
- **Merge into**: `develop`
- **Purpose**: New features or enhancements

#### Bugfix Branches
- **Naming**: `bugfix/<ticket-number>-<short-description>` or `bugfix/<short-description>`
- **Examples**: 
  - `bugfix/RAG-456-fix-evaluation-crash`
  - `bugfix/streamlit-memory-leak`
- **Branch from**: `develop`
- **Merge into**: `develop`
- **Purpose**: Fix bugs in development

#### Release Branches
- **Naming**: `release/<version>` (e.g., `release/v1.0.0`, `release/v1.2.0`)
- **Branch from**: `develop`
- **Merge into**: Both `main` and `develop`
- **Purpose**: Prepare for production release (version bumps, minor fixes, documentation)

#### Hotfix Branches
- **Naming**: `hotfix/<version>` or `hotfix/<short-description>`
- **Examples**: 
  - `hotfix/v1.0.1-critical-security-fix`
  - `hotfix/api-key-validation`
- **Branch from**: `main`
- **Merge into**: Both `main` and `develop`
- **Purpose**: Urgent fixes for production issues

## Workflow Commands

### Starting a New Feature
```bash
# Make sure develop is up to date
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop

# Create and switch to new feature branch
git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name

# Work on your feature...
git add .
git commit -m "feat: add document upload API endpoint"

# Push to remote
git push -u origin feature/your-feature-name
```

### Starting a Bugfix
```bash
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b bugfix/fix-description
# Make changes, commit, push
```

### Creating a Release
```bash
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b release/v1.0.0

# Update version numbers, CHANGELOG, etc.
git commit -m "chore: prepare release v1.0.0"

# Merge to main
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff release/v1.0.0
git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "Release version 1.0.0"
git push origin main --tags

# Merge back to develop
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff release/v1.0.0
git push origin develop

# Delete release branch
git branch -d release/v1.0.0
```

### Creating a Hotfix
```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b hotfix/v1.0.1-fix-description

# Make urgent fix
git commit -m "fix: critical security vulnerability"

# Merge to main
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff hotfix/v1.0.1-fix-description
git tag -a v1.0.1 -m "Hotfix version 1.0.1"
git push origin main --tags

# Merge to develop
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff hotfix/v1.0.1-fix-description
git push origin develop

# Delete hotfix branch
git branch -d hotfix/v1.0.1-fix-description
```

## Commit Message Standards

### Format
```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

### Types
- **feat**: New feature
- **fix**: Bug fix
- **docs**: Documentation changes
- **style**: Code style changes (formatting, no logic change)
- **refactor**: Code refactoring (no feature change)
- **perf**: Performance improvements
- **test**: Adding or updating tests
- **chore**: Build tasks, dependencies, etc.
- **ci**: CI/CD changes

### Examples
```bash
# Feature
git commit -m "feat(backend): add FastAPI document upload endpoint"

# Bug fix
git commit -m "fix(evaluation): resolve memory leak in RAGAS evaluation"

# Documentation
git commit -m "docs(readme): update installation instructions"

# Refactor
git commit -m "refactor(services): extract retrieval system factory"

# With body and breaking change
git commit -m "feat(api): migrate from Streamlit to FastAPI

- Add REST API endpoints
- Implement HTTP polling for real-time updates
- Add Pydantic models for validation

BREAKING CHANGE: Streamlit app is deprecated, use new API"
```

## Pull Request Guidelines

### Before Creating PR
1. Ensure your branch is up to date with target branch
2. Run all tests locally
3. Fix any linting errors
4. Update documentation if needed

### PR Title Format
Use same convention as commit messages:
- `feat: Add document processing API`
- `fix: Resolve evaluation timeout issue`
- `docs: Update API documentation`

### PR Description Template
```markdown
## Description
Brief description of what this PR does

## Type of Change
- [ ] Bug fix
- [ ] New feature
- [ ] Breaking change
- [ ] Documentation update

## Related Issue
Fixes #<issue-number>

## Changes Made
- Change 1
- Change 2
- Change 3

## Testing
- [ ] Unit tests added/updated
- [ ] Integration tests pass
- [ ] Manual testing completed

## Checklist
- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines
- [ ] Self-review completed
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No new warnings introduced
- [ ] Tests added for new features
```

### Review Process
- At least 1 approval required before merging
- All CI/CD checks must pass
- Resolve all comments before merging
- Use **Squash and Merge** for feature branches
- Use **Merge Commit** for release and hotfix branches

## Branch Protection Rules

### Main Branch
- ✅ Require pull request reviews (1+ approvals)
- ✅ Require status checks to pass
- ✅ Require branches to be up to date
- ✅ Do not allow force pushes
- ✅ Do not allow deletions

### Develop Branch
- ✅ Require pull request reviews
- ✅ Require status checks to pass
- ⚠️ Allow force pushes with lease (use carefully)
- ✅ Do not allow deletions

## Best Practices

### DO
✅ Keep commits small and focused
✅ Write descriptive commit messages
✅ Pull latest changes before starting work
✅ Rebase feature branches on develop regularly
✅ Delete branches after merging
✅ Tag releases with semantic versioning
✅ Update CHANGELOG.md for releases
✅ Run tests before pushing
✅ Review your own code before requesting review

### DON'T
❌ Commit directly to main or develop
❌ Force push to shared branches (except with --force-with-lease)
❌ Commit secrets, API keys, or .env files
❌ Merge without review (unless hotfix emergency)
❌ Leave WIP commits in PR history
❌ Ignore merge conflicts
❌ Push broken code
❌ Commit commented-out code (remove it)
❌ Use vague commit messages like "fix stuff" or "updates"

## Semantic Versioning

Format: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (e.g., `v1.2.3`)

- **MAJOR**: Breaking changes (v1.0.0 → v2.0.0)
- **MINOR**: New features, backwards compatible (v1.0.0 → v1.1.0)
- **PATCH**: Bug fixes, backwards compatible (v1.0.0 → v1.0.1)

### Examples
- `v0.1.0` - Initial development
- `v1.0.0` - First stable release
- `v1.1.0` - Add FastAPI backend (new feature)
- `v1.1.1` - Fix evaluation bug (patch)
- `v2.0.0` - Remove Streamlit support (breaking change)

## Project-Specific Workflow

### Converting Streamlit to FastAPI + React

#### Phase 1: Backend Setup
```bash
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/backend-setup

# Create backend structure
# Commit incrementally
git commit -m "feat(backend): initialize FastAPI project structure"
git commit -m "feat(backend): add Pydantic models"
git commit -m "feat(backend): implement document upload endpoint"

git push -u origin feature/backend-setup
# Create PR to develop
```

#### Phase 2: Frontend Setup
```bash
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/frontend-setup

# Create Next.js project
git commit -m "feat(frontend): initialize Next.js 14 with TypeScript"
git commit -m "feat(frontend): setup Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui"
git commit -m "feat(frontend): create API client"

git push -u origin feature/frontend-setup
# Create PR to develop
```

#### Phase 3: Feature Migration
Each feature gets its own branch:
- `feature/document-upload-ui`
- `feature/evaluation-engine-api`
- `feature/results-visualization`
- `feature/http-polling-updates`

## Emergency Procedures

### Rollback Production
```bash
# Find the last good commit
git log --oneline

# Create hotfix to revert
git checkout main
git checkout -b hotfix/rollback-to-v1.0.0
git revert <bad-commit-hash>
git push -u origin hotfix/rollback-to-v1.0.0

# Follow hotfix merge process
```

### Fix Accidentally Committed Secrets
```bash
# Remove from history (USE WITH CAUTION)
git filter-branch --force --index-filter \
  "git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch .env" \
  --prune-empty --tag-name-filter cat -- --all

# Force push (coordinate with team)
git push origin --force --all

# Immediately rotate compromised credentials
```

## Helpful Git Commands

### Sync Feature Branch with Develop
```bash
git checkout feature/your-feature
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/develop
# Resolve conflicts if any
git push --force-with-lease
```

### Undo Last Commit (Not Pushed)
```bash
git reset --soft HEAD~1  # Keep changes staged
git reset HEAD~1          # Keep changes unstaged
git reset --hard HEAD~1   # Discard changes (CAREFUL!)
```

### View Branch History
```bash
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all
```

### Stash Changes Temporarily
```bash
git stash save "WIP: working on evaluation"
git checkout another-branch
git checkout feature/your-feature
git stash pop
```

### Clean Up Local Branches
```bash
# Delete merged branches
git branch --merged | grep -v "\*\|main\|develop" | xargs -n 1 git branch -d

# Prune remote-tracking branches
git fetch --prune
```
